{
  "children": [
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            49,
            80
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Reading a chart without a mouse"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 1,
      "position": [
        47,
        80
      ],
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            82,
            361
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The normative requirement is an equivalence: keyboard focus MUST produce the\nsame readout as hover. Not a similar one, not an abbreviated one — the same,\nfrom the same formatting path, because two paths are two things to keep in\nstep and one of them will eventually be forgotten."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        82,
        361
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            363,
            374
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "A chart is "
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "position": [
                376,
                379
              ],
              "type": "text",
              "value": "one"
            }
          ],
          "position": [
            374,
            381
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            381,
            610
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " tab stop, never one per mark. Arrow keys walk the focus\norder from there, Home and End jump to its ends, Page Up and Page Down move\nbetween series, Enter and Space select, Escape drops the readout without\nleaving the chart, and "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            610,
            613
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "T"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            613,
            781
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " toggles the table view. Fifteen data points would\notherwise be fifteen tab stops, and a page of charts would be unusable by\nexactly the reader the contract exists for."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        363,
        781
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
