    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            943,
            1343
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "This case is here to name the contract, not to prove it. Keyboard navigation\nis behaviour over time — a key arrives, a readout changes — and a golden is one\ndocument frozen at one instant, so no file in this directory can hold the\nevidence. The corpus renders with the interaction layer off on purpose, since\nthe hit-rect overlay belongs to a live document and would pin nothing but its\nown geometry."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        943,
        1343
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            1345,
            1379
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "So the requirement is declared in "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            1379,
            1390
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "meta.json"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            1390,
            1536
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " rather than derived, which is the\none honest way to record it: the executable evidence is the interaction layer's\nown tests, where a synthesised "
        },
        {
          "position": [
            1536,
            1548
          ],
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "ArrowRight"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            1548,
            1631
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": " and a synthesised pointer move are\nasserted to produce the identical readout rows."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        1345,
        1631
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
